# Translation Consistency Guidelines

This project is a Japanese translation/adaptation of the official Sui Move intro course maintained by Sui Foundation. This repository is forked from the original English content at [https://github.com/sui-foundation/sui-move-intro-course](https://github.com/sui-foundation/sui-move-intro-course).

**Source Repository**: [sui-foundation/sui-move-intro-course](https://github.com/sui-foundation/sui-move-intro-course)
**Target Repository**: Japanese translation (this repository)

Maintain consistency and quality across all translated materials while preserving educational value and technical accuracy.

## Translation Principles

### Language Strategy

- **Primary Language**: Japanese for all lesson content and explanations
- **Technical Terms**: Use English terms with Japanese explanations in parentheses on first mention
- **Code Comments**: Keep in English (industry standard)
- **Variable/Function Names**: Keep original English names for consistency with Sui ecosystem

### Terminology Consistency

#### Core Sui Concepts (English → Japanese)

- **Object** → オブジェクト
- **Ownership** → 所有権 (ownership)
- **Shared Object** → 共有オブジェクト (shared object)
- **Immutable** → 不変 (immutable)
- **Transaction Context** → トランザクションコンテキスト (transaction context)
- **Witness Pattern** → ウィットネスパターン (witness pattern)
- **Capability** → ケイパビリティ (capability)
- **Dynamic Field** → 動的フィールド (dynamic field)
- **Hot Potato** → ホットポテト (hot potato)
- **One-Time Witness** → ワンタイムウィットネス (one-time witness)

#### Move Language Terms

- **Module** → モジュール (module)
- **Function** → 関数 (function)
- **Struct** → 構造体 (struct)
- **Ability** → アビリティ (ability)
- **Generic** → ジェネリック (generic)
- **Entry Function** → エントリー関数 (entry function)
- **Public Function** → パブリック関数 (public function)

## Content Structure

### Lesson Files (`lessons/*.md`)

````markdown
# レッスンタイトル (Lesson Title)

## 学習目標 (Learning Objectives)

- 日本語での目標説明
- English technical concepts in parentheses

## 概念説明 (Concept Explanation)

詳細な日本語説明と technical terms (英語専門用語)

## コード例 (Code Examples)

\```move
// English comments in code
public entry fun example_function(ctx: &mut TxContext) {
// Implementation
}
\```

## まとめ (Summary)

重要なポイントの日本語まとめ
````

### Exercise Files (`exercises/`)

- **Problem Statements**: In Japanese with clear objectives
- **Code Templates**: English variable names, Japanese comments where helpful
- **Answer Keys**: Japanese explanations with technical reasoning

## Translation Quality Standards

### Consistency Checks

- Use consistent terminology across all files
- Maintain parallel structure with English source when applicable
- Keep technical accuracy while making content accessible to Japanese learners

### Cultural Adaptation

- Use Japanese learning conventions (numbered steps, clear sections)
- Include cultural context for DeFi/blockchain concepts when helpful
- Adapt examples to be relevant for Japanese developers

### Source Repository Tracking

- **Monitor Updates**: Regularly check [source repository](https://github.com/sui-foundation/sui-move-intro-course) for updates
- **Version Tracking**: Document which version/commit of the source is being translated
- **Change Detection**: Use git diff/compare to identify specific changes in source content
- **Update Priority**: Focus on technical accuracy updates and new educational content

### Future Translation Workflow

1. **Source Update**: When English content updates, identify changed sections
2. **Translation Planning**: Review technical terms and maintain terminology consistency
3. **Content Adaptation**: Translate while preserving educational progression
4. **Review Process**: Verify technical accuracy and language quality
5. **Cross-Reference Update**: Update internal links and references
6. **Sync Verification**: Ensure translated content matches source structure and learning objectives

## File Organization for Translation

### Parallel Structure

- Maintain same directory structure as English source
- Keep same file names for easy cross-reference
- Use git history to track translation progress

### Version Management

- Document source version being translated
- Track translation completion status
- Note any adaptations or additions for Japanese audience

## Code Documentation Translation

### Move Code Comments

```move
/// Creates a new transcript object
/// 新しい成績証明書オブジェクトを作成します
public fun create_transcript(
    student_name: String, // 学生名
    ctx: &mut TxContext
): Transcript {
    // Implementation...
}
```

### Error Messages

- Keep error constants in English for debugging
- Add Japanese comments explaining error conditions
- Document error handling patterns in Japanese

This rule ensures consistent, high-quality Japanese content that serves Japanese learners while maintaining technical accuracy and ecosystem compatibility.
